            <ArticleTitle>Two novel clinical presentations of Burkholderia cepacia infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3904-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two cases of multidrug-resistant Burkholderia cepacia (B. cepacia genomovar I) and Burkholderia multivorans causing multiple liver abscesses in a patient with bronchial asthma (case 1) and peritonitis in a patient with cirrhosis and hepatitis C virus disease (case 2), respectively. Both patients were treated successfully.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
